WEBVTT

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:08.440
<i>Morning has arrived.</i>

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:12.820
<i>The refreshing morning of the highlands...</i>

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:17.320
<i>The final morning.</i>

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:25.990
Sorry, Aya-chan.

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:27.540
Did you turn off my alarm?

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:34.910
Aya-chan, it's time.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:38.020
I know. I'm getting up.

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:40.040
But first, three more minutes.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.140
No.

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:44.640
<i>It's their second Inter-High.</i>

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:48.070
<i>Everyone's trained as hard as they can.</i>

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:51.650
<i>They didn't waste even a second.</i>

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:56.520
<i>New students joined the club. 
They became second-years.</i>

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:59.910
<i>Summer came. They went through 
some difficult times.</i>

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:03.060
<i>They've gotten so much stronger.</i>

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:05.160
<i>They were strong during the race.</i>

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:11.420
<i>But at this year's Inter-High, they still 
haven't won a single colored number tag.</i>

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:14.740
<i>Today is the final race.</i>

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:17.910
<i>The final day of their 
Inter-High as second-years.</i>

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:21.410
<i>I hope their final wish comes true.</i>

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:24.680
<i>All I can do is cheer them on
 and support them, but...</i>

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:30.600
<i>Good luck, Team Sohoku!</i>

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:31.980
<b>Inter-High Road Race</b>

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:44.500
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:08.020
<i>LINE.25  Their Respective Starting Lines</i>

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:08.950
<b>Boys' Inter-High Road Race Day 3</b>

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:14.020
They're here!

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:15.210
They've arrived!

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:16.630
The champions, Hakone Academy!

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:18.880
Hakone Academy!

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:20.890
Win today's race, too!

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:22.690
Hakone Academy!

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:25.610
Izumida-kun, yesterday's race was close.

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:29.290
But Hakone Academy was the only team 
to send two riders to the finish line.

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:31.300
You were in perfect form.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.090
Yes.

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:35.230
It's too bad you failed to 
get all three number tags.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:36.410
Do you think you'll do it today?

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:40.370
The overall winner of the Inter-High 
will be decided at today's finish line.

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:45.370
If there are teams hoping to win the 
sprint or mountain line, let them know

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:47.160
that they can have them.

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:53.000
Hakone Academy will be competing only for the
 final finish line and its yellow number tag.

00:03:58.290 --> 00:03:59.640
Only the finish line?

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:04.210
Hakone Academy's putting their 
efforts toward it from the start.

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:07.970
Taking the finish line and 
reclaiming of their throne.

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:11.300
We'll give up everything today, Yuki.

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:14.460
<i>Give up everything?</i>

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:16.850
<i>Touichirou, does that mean you...</i>

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:20.730
It's my final job as team captain, Yuki.

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:22.610
Touichirou...

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:24.530
We are...

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:25.530
Yeah.

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:27.300
...strong!

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.410
For sure!

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:31.870
<i>We have to win.</i>

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:41.450
Manami's late.

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:47.670
I overslept.

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:51.060
<b>Chiba
Sohoku High School</b>

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:53.230
Let's go, Sohoku!

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:01.000
This is the end. We made it to the final day.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.840
The six of us. We all made it together.

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:04.660
Naruko!

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:05.560
Yeah!

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:06.250
Imaizumi!

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:07.090
Yeah!

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:07.740
Onoda!

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:08.510
Yes, sir!

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:09.290
Kaburagi!

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:09.870
Yes, sir!

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:11.460
And Aoyagi!

00:05:13.490 --> 00:05:15.320
Do you believe in miracles?

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:23.050
Today's our last chance to set off
 everything we've built up.

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:26.190
Even if we give everything we've got 
and collapse at the finish line,

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:28.530
our faith in miracles will take us there.

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:32.180
We'll keep our faith alive.

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:35.310
If one of us ends up in a race of 
centimeters before the final finish line...

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:38.190
That faith will push him across it!

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:40.810
<i>Junta!</i>

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:42.070
<i>Teshima-san!</i>

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:44.100
<i>Of course.</i>

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:45.220
<i>Teshima-san!</i>

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:49.160
Let's go! This is our last race!

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:50.570
Sohoku!

00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:51.660
Fight!

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.330
Yeah!

00:05:57.590 --> 00:06:00.600
Give it everything you've 
got again this year.

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:04.510
We will.

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:06.370
We're counting on your support!

00:06:06.370 --> 00:06:07.010
Got it!

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:08.680
Thank you!

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:11.050
We'll be back.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:12.580
Thanks!

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:14.410
Aoyagi-san...

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:18.450
Are your legs okay?

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:21.480
You noticed.

00:06:22.170 --> 00:06:23.650
I am the team's manager.

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:27.290
Don't push yourself too hard during the race.

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:29.480
Though I doubt you can't.

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:34.370
All the braces and painkillers in 
the first-aid box were missing.

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:35.800
I had no choice.

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:38.870
I still have a job left to do.

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:44.400
You don't need to worry.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:47.800
I'm standing at the final stage of 
the Inter-High wearing the jersey

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:49.680
I've admired for three years.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:51.130
That's enough for me.

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:55.290
All of my wishes have already come true.

00:06:56.270 --> 00:07:03.440
<i>The third and final day of the Tochigi 
Inter-High Road Race begins in ten minutes.</i>

00:06:57.790 --> 00:07:03.440
<b>Boys' Inter-High Road Race Day 3</b>

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:05.030
Hakone Academy!

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:06.410
Go, champs!

00:07:06.410 --> 00:07:07.860
Kanagawa's the best!

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:09.560
Sohoku!

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:10.840
You can do it, Chiba!

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:12.360
We're rooting for you this year, too!

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:16.100
I've never seen a first-year start 
first for Hakone Academy before!

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:19.850
At the Inter-High, they start in the 
order they finished on the previous day.

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:23.560
Isn't that the younger brother 
of last year's #4, Shinkai?

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:25.040
Damn! He seems strong!

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:26.420
Ready, and...

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:29.210
Onoda-kun, good luck!

00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:31.370
We hope you take first again this year!

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:32.010
Huh?

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:33.000
Huh?

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:35.430
Huh? What?!

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:36.990
Ready, and...

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:38.810
Onoda-kun, you can do it!

00:07:39.130 --> 00:07:42.640
I can't, I can't, I can't, 
I can't, I can't...

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:41.530
He's so cute!

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:42.640
He's embarrassed!

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:44.980
Please don't set your expectations that high.

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:46.400
You can't? What's wrong with you?

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:47.770
I can't, I can't, I can't...

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:50.870
He fell!

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:52.700
Look! Sohoku fell!

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:54.660
He fell before the race started!

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:57.600
It feels like you do the 
same thing every year.

00:07:57.600 --> 00:07:58.660
S-Sorry.

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:00.990
The way he gets up is so cute!

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:03.290
There's no getting through to them.

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:04.540
Just ignore them.

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:06.670
What? But I'd feel bad.

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:16.720
<i>My heart won't stop pounding.</i>

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:19.470
<i>This is crazy. It's my third and final—</i>

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:20.310
<i>No...</i>

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:23.890
<i>It's because it's my first 
and final Inter-High.</i>

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:28.690
<i>I longed to race in the Inter-High.</i>

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:32.930
<i>I fought hard, but failed 
to qualify in my second year.</i>

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:35.690
<i>Even after becoming captain in my third year,</i>

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:41.000
<i>I finally earned an Inter-High number 
tag only after desperately hanging on.</i>

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:46.660
<i>My legs and arms are shaking.</i>

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:49.130
<i>My heart is so small.</i>

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:51.850
<i>The Inter-High is ending.</i>

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:56.500
<i>My fate and Sohoku's will be decided today.</i>

00:08:58.360 --> 00:08:59.540
<i>It's the final day.</i>

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:05.330
<i>Everything I've done and built up 
these past three years.</i>

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:07.380
<i>The sky's so bright.</i>

00:09:07.990 --> 00:09:10.570
<i>That sky is connected to today's finish line.</i>

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:12.960
<i>The finish line lies beyond it.</i>

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:14.320
<i>But...</i>

00:09:15.370 --> 00:09:19.070
<i>I probably won't be able to finish today.</i>

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:21.080
<i>That's fine, though.</i>

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:25.640
<i>As long as someone entrusted 
with our jersey makes it...</i>

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:29.170
<i>As long as I can see the finish line 
through his eyes, it's fine.</i>

00:09:29.990 --> 00:09:32.170
<i>Let's go, Teshima Junta.</i>

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:34.000
<i>I am an ordinary man.</i>

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:37.180
<i>I have no exceptional skill or talent, but...</i>

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:40.180
<i>I've worked hard!</i>

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:43.100
<i>Along with my five teammates,</i>

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:48.650
<i>we'll beat you and Hakone Academy, Shikiba!</i>

00:09:52.970 --> 00:09:54.360
<i>Ashikiba...</i>

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:56.320
<i>Jun-chan.</i>

00:09:57.380 --> 00:09:58.700
Bring it on.

00:10:00.650 --> 00:10:01.740
What?

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:02.660
Huh?

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:05.910
What's up?

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:08.880
Who are you talking to, Takuto? Fairies?

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:13.870
I thought Jun-chan said something, 
so I responded to him.

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:15.560
He didn't say anything.

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:16.210
I see.

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:18.470
<i>Shikiba's amazing.</i>

00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:21.880
<i>His senses are honed.</i>

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:23.350
<i>Everyone calls him an airhead,</i>

00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:27.350
<i>but during a race, that becomes
 an immeasurable power.</i>

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:29.850
<b>Inter-High Road Race</b>

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:29.850
<i>The race will begin in five minutes.</i>

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:32.630
I'm starting to get nervous!

00:10:32.630 --> 00:10:35.650
Why are you getting nervous? 
You're not racing!

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:36.900
Yeah, but still!

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:40.920
Anyway, it's been bothering me, 
but isn't something missing?

00:10:40.920 --> 00:10:42.020
What's missing?

00:10:42.020 --> 00:10:43.810
One of the teams.

00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:46.910
Yesterday's winner. The team that 
took first on the second day,

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:48.660
Kyoto Fushimi.

00:10:50.050 --> 00:10:51.500
With only five minutes to spare!

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:55.450
Yesterday's winning team, 
Kyoto Fushimi, has arrived!

00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:59.380
Excuse us.

00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:00.490
What is that?

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:01.620
Look at that!

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:02.180
Whoa!

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:05.690
There's no reason to act so surprised.

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:08.810
We just shed a little weight.

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:13.230
The entire Kyoto Fushimi 
team shaved their heads!

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:15.480
Throw it away, throw it away...

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:21.370
Your useless pride, your useless 
celebratory mood, your useless showing off.

00:11:21.370 --> 00:11:24.890
With victory right before our eyes...

00:11:25.880 --> 00:11:28.500
We must throw everything away!

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:31.490
They won yesterday and are starting first!

00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:33.000
But they're still willing to go that far?

00:11:36.970 --> 00:11:38.960
We'll take today, too.

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:40.970
<i>Midousuji-kun...</i>

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:49.910
<b>Inter-High
 Road Race</b>

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:48.130
<i>The race will begin in one minute!</i>

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:55.860
<b>Sohoku High School</b>

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:58.320
<b>Hakone Academy</b>

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:00.780
<b>Kyoto Fushimi</b>

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:02.780
<b>Kumamoto Daiichi</b>

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:09.610
<i>Once we cross this starting line,
the final day of the Inter-High will begin.</i>

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:15.250
<i>The third and final day of the Inter-High</i>

00:12:15.590 --> 00:12:16.970
<i>begins now!</i>

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:21.800
Go, Kyoto Fushimi!

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:22.760
Hakone Academy!

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:25.000
Don't let them beat you, Sohoku!

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:27.600
<i>The riders are starting one after another.</i>

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:33.880
They're starting already?

00:12:33.880 --> 00:12:35.370
That's not good.

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:38.270
I'm totally late.

00:12:38.740 --> 00:12:43.160
<i>The second day's fourth place finisher, 
#11 and Hakone Academy's ace,</i>

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:45.590
<i>Ashikiba, is starting.</i>

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:50.620
<i>Behind him are fifth and sixth,
 Kyoto Fushimi's Mizuta</i>

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:50.620
I'm Kyoto Fushimi's captain, Mizuta Nobuyuki!

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:54.710
<i>and last year's winner 
and #1, Sohoku's Onoda.</i>

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:52.920
Thank you!

00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:54.710
I'll do my best!

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:56.090
Forty seconds to go.

00:12:55.030 --> 00:12:56.080
Thank you!

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:57.750
I'm heading out.

00:12:57.750 --> 00:12:59.890
Got it. Hotshot's in the lead.

00:12:59.890 --> 00:13:00.960
Thirty seconds.

00:13:01.310 --> 00:13:04.360
You're starting before us.

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:06.800
Meet up with hotshot as soon as you can.

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:11.260
He might cry from loneliness if 
he's the only one who doesn't.

00:13:12.190 --> 00:13:13.130
Got it.

00:13:14.950 --> 00:13:16.730
Naruko-kun, please.

00:13:19.050 --> 00:13:19.980
Onoda-kun!

00:13:20.470 --> 00:13:22.570
Take my hopes with you!

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:24.310
My determination is yours!

00:13:24.310 --> 00:13:26.200
And take care of hotshot!

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:28.070
I will! Thanks!

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:30.890
We're counting on you, Onoda.

00:13:30.890 --> 00:13:31.370
Yes, sir!

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:33.870
We'll catch up soon. Wait for us.

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:35.870
Onoda-san, you've got this!

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:39.160
Go!

00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:39.880
Yes, sir!

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:43.340
<i>Mizuta and Onoda have started.</i>

00:13:46.280 --> 00:13:48.300
<i>I crossed the starting line.</i>

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:50.000
<i>The race has started.</i>

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:52.100
<i>The third and final day.</i>

00:13:52.870 --> 00:13:57.020
<i>I'm racing toward the finish line 
at the end of this road.</i>

00:13:57.720 --> 00:13:59.220
<i>My heart is pounding.</i>

00:13:59.220 --> 00:14:02.600
<i>I have only my body and legs 
to propel myself forward.</i>

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:05.700
<i>There's no guarantee I'll 
make it there in one piece.</i>

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:06.820
<i>So...</i>

00:14:07.480 --> 00:14:09.700
<i>I'll ride as hard as I can!</i>

00:14:15.190 --> 00:14:16.410
<i>Manami-kun!</i>

00:14:16.890 --> 00:14:18.580
I'll catch up to you later.

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:21.540
Let's meet again on 
the course, Sakamichi-kun.

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:26.880
Great. I was worried since 
I didn't see you, Manami-kun.

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:28.090
W-Were you in the bathroom?

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:29.840
No, I overslept.

00:14:30.460 --> 00:14:33.650
<i>He overslept? Sounds like him.</i>

00:14:34.420 --> 00:14:37.350
<i>I'm sure we'll meet again today somewhere.</i>

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:40.930
<i>Then let's ride together 
like we did last year!</i>

00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:46.230
#13, hurry.

00:14:46.540 --> 00:14:47.790
Sorry.

00:14:47.790 --> 00:14:50.110
What are you doing, Manami?

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:52.530
You're lucky we're starting in 
the order we finished, Manami.

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:55.410
Get in line. Don't scare us like that.

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:58.420
Are you at least focused?

00:14:58.420 --> 00:15:00.420
Yeah, totally.

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:03.250
Good.

00:15:03.860 --> 00:15:05.160
Let's go, Hakone Academy.

00:15:07.030 --> 00:15:08.090
Let's go.

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:13.380
This is the final first step we'll 
take towards reclaiming our throne!

00:15:13.380 --> 00:15:15.970
<i>The second pack will now start in order.</i>

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:17.890
Let's go, Sohoku!

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:22.890
We can't let Hakone Academy 
and hotshot hog the spotlight!

00:15:22.890 --> 00:15:26.360
Let's make a splash on the final day, guys!

00:15:27.620 --> 00:15:30.150
The final day of the Inter-High 
is finally starting!

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:32.480
It's my time to shine!

00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:35.200
I'm ready to go anytime! Just say the word!

00:15:35.650 --> 00:15:36.700
Don't go.

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:37.570
Yes, sir!

00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:40.290
Huh? What?

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:42.100
You just told me to go.

00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:43.720
I said don't go.

00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:45.190
As in "do not."

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:47.460
Oh, <i>don't</i> go.

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:48.670
<i>He's an idiot.</i>

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:53.090
Morph, morph, morph!

00:15:53.410 --> 00:15:55.610
The lead pack's here! He's saying "morph!"

00:15:55.610 --> 00:15:56.680
Morph!

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:58.560
It's yesterday's winners, Kyoto Fushimi!

00:15:58.960 --> 00:16:04.230
Kyoto Fushimi's Midousuji is wearing the 
previous day's winner's yellow number tag!

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:07.410
That unconventional award 
ceremony was the best!

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:09.000
You can do it, Kyoto Fushimi!

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:10.110
Kyoto!

00:16:12.440 --> 00:16:13.930
<i>Midousuji...</i>

00:16:13.930 --> 00:16:18.210
<i>He won over the fans with the second day's 
victory and his performance.</i>

00:16:18.210 --> 00:16:20.790
<i>The atmosphere has changed 
completely since yesterday.</i>

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:22.770
We hope you win again today!

00:16:22.770 --> 00:16:24.530
You've got this, Kyoto Fushimi!

00:16:24.530 --> 00:16:26.210
<i>It's harder for us now.</i>

00:16:29.290 --> 00:16:31.210
<i>You just wait, Imaizumi-kun.</i>

00:16:31.810 --> 00:16:34.870
<i>Today's course starts by 
taking us around the lake.</i>

00:16:35.290 --> 00:16:39.470
<i>It's not too long, but it's 
a fairly long, flat road.</i>

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:42.290
<i>I need to catch up here.</i>

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:44.230
<i>Around now, at the front...</i>

00:16:57.620 --> 00:16:59.640
I caught up, Yuto.

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:01.750
That was quick, Ashikiba-san.

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:05.830
<i>Third-year and ace Ashikiba-san 
and first-year Shinkai Yuto-kun.</i>

00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:11.840
<i>Against to Hakone Academy's two, 
Sohoku has only Imaizumi-kun.</i>

00:17:13.690 --> 00:17:15.470
How do you feel?

00:17:17.170 --> 00:17:18.680
Not bad.

00:17:19.880 --> 00:17:21.350
<i>Damn.</i>

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:25.100
<i>I can't believe yesterday's 
results created this situation.</i>

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:26.910
<i>Is he here yet?</i>

00:17:26.910 --> 00:17:29.610
<i>Come quickly, Onoda!</i>

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:32.690
I see him. It's Imaizumi-kun!

00:17:33.210 --> 00:17:35.110
<i>He's still pretty far ahead.</i>

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:38.110
But I'll get there!

00:17:40.920 --> 00:17:42.370
What?!

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:47.870
<i>I'll definitely catch up.</i>

00:17:48.760 --> 00:17:49.970
<i>Imaizumi-kun!</i>

00:17:55.240 --> 00:18:00.770
<i>Since meeting you and learning about the 
world of bicycle racing, I've changed.</i>

00:18:04.970 --> 00:18:07.600
<i>I'd never played a sport before.</i>

00:18:08.210 --> 00:18:12.440
<i>I met so many people after 
joining the bicycle racing club.</i>

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:21.070
<i>Kinjou-san taught me how Team Sohoku never 
gives up and always supports each other.</i>

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:25.140
You don't need to try so hard by yourself.

00:18:25.720 --> 00:18:28.040
If you fall, I will support you.

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:33.450
But if someone else should fall,
 you must support them.

00:18:34.390 --> 00:18:36.290
That is Team Sohoku.

00:18:36.290 --> 00:18:37.810
That's how we ride.

00:18:40.170 --> 00:18:46.580
<i>The strong-willed and determined 
Tadokoro-san taught me to ride single-mindedly.</i>

00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:53.270
I am eternally grateful enough to you.

00:18:53.910 --> 00:18:54.930
Onoda...

00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:57.400
Thank you.

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:07.930
I didn't think I'd get to see those jerseys
 with my own eyes again...

00:19:08.920 --> 00:19:10.080
I'm back!

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:12.790
Team Sohoku!

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:19.420
<i>Makishima-san taught me the difficulty, 
fun, and coolness of climbing.</i>

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:22.470
I understand...

00:19:23.830 --> 00:19:25.930
I'm a climber, too.

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:27.410
What?

00:19:27.410 --> 00:19:29.850
You just have to ride.

00:19:30.280 --> 00:19:34.230
On a bicycle, the more you pedal,
 the stronger you'll become.

00:19:35.830 --> 00:19:40.250
<i>Sugimoto-kun, Koga-san, 
Kanzaki-san, and Tachibana-san...</i>

00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:44.070
<i>They're all important members of Team Sohoku.</i>

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:47.620
<i>No, that's not all.</i>

00:19:50.020 --> 00:19:53.320
<i>Manami-kun and the other 
members of Hakone Academy...</i>

00:19:55.850 --> 00:19:58.310
<i>Midousuji-kun and the rest of Kyoto Fushimi...</i>

00:20:00.230 --> 00:20:06.440
<i>Everyone riding on this course 
right now is so fast and strong,</i>

00:20:07.010 --> 00:20:11.170
<i>but they're all friends I've met 
because I starting cycling.</i>

00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:26.280
<i>So I'll ride as hard as I can!</i>

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:30.550
<i>Teshima-san wore himself 
down fighting against</i>

00:20:30.550 --> 00:20:34.080
<i>Manami-kun and sent us his 
passionate vibrations.</i>

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:41.630
<i>Naruko-kun pursued Hakone 
Academy and Kyoto Fushimi,</i>

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:44.380
<i>and he clung to the lead pack alone 
until we could rejoin him.</i>

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:54.560
<i>Kaburagi-kun pushed himself so hard in a 
sprint for the first day's first result</i>

00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:57.060
<i>that he collapsed after he finished.</i>

00:21:00.310 --> 00:21:04.990
<i>And when Kaburagi-kun stopped 
pedaling on the second day,</i>

00:21:05.460 --> 00:21:08.560
<i>Aoyagi-san went to get him and 
brought him back to the team.</i>

00:21:16.600 --> 00:21:18.880
<i>For all those people!</i>

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:22.730
<i>For Team Sohoku, I ride!</i>

00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:33.680
Just you wait, Imaizumi-kun!

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:40.480
Onoda!

00:21:41.010 --> 00:21:44.180
Let's go to the finish line, Imaizumi-kun!

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:55.000
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:21:50.790 --> 00:21:54.170
I'll pedal as hard as I can!

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:29.970
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.
